I have not one clue what your intentions are here.
That seems to have nothing to do with being blind,
as you don't specify _being blind_, just bringing
along a potion of blindness.

In English, one would most likely say "turn on the
lamp"; even in NetHack, "put on" means something you
do with rings, amulets, towels, lenses, blindfolds
and such, not lamps. Lamps get a)pplied to turn them
on.

The "quiver the potion" makes no sense to me.  Even
if it were possible, what good would quivering a
potion do?

Did you mean "quaff the potion"? That makes sense,
in terms of something one would normally do in a
game of NetHack, and it makes the PC blind, the
intention of your test.

But now the behavior you describe for the display of
which locations are lighted is exactly the behavior
an experienced NetHack player would expect, and as
I've described it a couple of times now: the map
seen by the player shows what the blind PC
_remembers_, not necessarily what the situation
currently _is_.

